                    {
                        "form_id": "3c699e4b-f598-4ed8-a38b-30a711e31cdd",
                        "entry_id": "ce884cc8-9fdc-3f84-acd7-966d0cfb7622",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "losels"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3b5d5188-d1c4-34e8-b025-3b10d467e1dd",
                        "entry_id": "ce884cc8-9fdc-3f84-acd7-966d0cfb7622",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A worthless or despicable person, scoundrel."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d823247-b99c-4b04-b729-3c036ff54ff2",
                                "sense_id": "3b5d5188-d1c4-34e8-b025-3b10d467e1dd",
                                "text": "Dowtles such losels\nMake the churche to be\nIn smale auctoryte; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a63e459-b8d0-41fa-8e92-319bf49feae7",
                                "sense_id": "3b5d5188-d1c4-34e8-b025-3b10d467e1dd",
                                "text": "The whiles a losell wandring by the way, / One that to bountie neuer cast his mind, / Ne thought of honour euer did assay […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b6944d0-13ba-4541-9dd9-3cea91f23f13",
                                "sense_id": "3b5d5188-d1c4-34e8-b025-3b10d467e1dd",
                                "text": "And, losel, thou art worthy to be hang'd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82580b06-3816-4a81-95d1-e34fb0a9e951",
                                "sense_id": "3b5d5188-d1c4-34e8-b025-3b10d467e1dd",
                                "text": "These thousand straight-standing firm-set individuals, who shoulder arms, who march, wheel, advance, retreat; and are, for your behoof, a magazine charged with fiery death, in the most perfect condition of potential activity: few months ago, till the persuasive sergeant came, what were they? Multiform ragged losels, runaway apprentices, starved weavers, thievish valets […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "312fc33e-69ae-4fe4-8bc7-58e2924365b0",
                                "sense_id": "3b5d5188-d1c4-34e8-b025-3b10d467e1dd",
                                "text": "Not since I backed a horse have I been pressed so hard; peril of life, jeopardy of land and livelihood, and to sum up, all these losels in the wood to hunt me down."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "543bb5af-b684-42e8-9a5a-2a47ed37f53d",
                                "sense_id": "3b5d5188-d1c4-34e8-b025-3b10d467e1dd",
                                "text": "Lots of folk live on their wits: / Lecturers, lispers, / Losels, loblolly-men, louts— / They don't end up as paupers; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "767db8e9-9ba6-4af5-9154-e4e0d8ae04c6",
                                "sense_id": "3b5d5188-d1c4-34e8-b025-3b10d467e1dd",
                                "text": "‘Come on, you losel,’ he said to Spatchcock, ‘you privy calligrapher, you. You can carry his bottles. I’ll carry him.’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
